erlang:memory(code) is a whole-node counter over coarse-grained allocations
and includes per-module metadata, not only JIT-emitted instructions. It counts
a DIFFERENT thing from the .beam bytes in section 1. Read a per-module guard
cost out of it ONLY if the two U->G steps agree with each other AND the two
same-kind, different-position comparisons are near zero.

